replies.body:
@pete-gov  + @ElaineFR  - Apologies for chiming in here - Thanks a lot for this ask / response - it might not be entirely related to the 20x - but rather to the Rev 5 Class D Consolidated rules - one additional clarifying question I would like to have to this topic. In the following RFC (https://www.fedramp.gov/rfcs/0030/ ) there was a mention about particular STIG / CIS levels related to "SA-04(5): Acquisition Process | System, Component, and Service Configurations" - and basically in case of lack of STIG the CIS L1 + L2 rules would be sufficient. When I look at the current wording in the consolidated rules - I can't really find a reference to STIG or CIS Level 1 / 2 rules - so I am trying to understand from an Operating Systems perspective what would be a sufficient set of secure configurations for Rev 5 Class D? I understand there are different ways to ensure secure configuration - but it could be described in 20 - 50 or 300 rules.

We are aiming for a CIS benchmark anyways - the questions is whether that would be sufficient with L1 only rules or in that case L1 + L2 would make the mark... 

Appreciate your response in advance!

@pallakatos - first note is, RFCs are proposals that are irrelevant the moment they close. Never refer to them afterwards except to review any linked outcome. In this case, you'd want to start with [NTC-0013](https://www.fedramp.gov/notices/0013/) (linked at the very top of the old RFC page) and catch up from there.

The finalized control guidance for CR26 is built into the CR26 JSON data and has a human-readable version here: https://www.fedramp.gov/2026/providers/rev5/controls/

You'll note there is no SA-04 guidance. We have removed FedRAMP-specific guidance requiring STIG / CIS benchmarks. Document the choices you make and why they meet the control.

@pete-gov, with the RAR/SAR/SAP path, we have our package completely built. We obtained fedramp equivalency, as well. I think it would be faster for us to initially adopt the Rev 5 approach and then move to 20x later. 

That said, does Rev 5 still require a sponsor to get listed? If so, we may need to rethink. 

Thanks for any insights! 🙏🏻
